wl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19022770\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hematopoietic_stem_cell\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000037 \"A stem cell from which all cells of the lymphoid and myeloid lineages develop, including blood cells and cells of the immune system. Hematopoietic stem cells lack cell markers of effector cells (lin-negative). Lin-negative is defined by lacking one or more of the following cell surface markers: CD2, CD3 epsilon, CD4, CD5 ,CD8 alpha chain, CD11b, CD14, CD19, CD20, CD56, ly6G, ter119.\")\n\n  Line 4088: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721601464\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000038 \"A progenitor cell committed to the erythroid lineage.\")\n\n  Line 4103: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721662544\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000039 \"A cell that is within the developmental lineage of gametes and is able to pass along its genetic material to offspring.\")\n\n  Line 4112: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:1104740\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monoblast\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.copewithcytokines.de\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000040 \"A myeloid progenitor cell committed to the monocyte lineage. This cell is CD11b-positive, has basophilic cytoplasm, euchromatin, and the presence of a nucleolus.\")\n\n  Line 4127: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721601464\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.cap.org\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000041 \"A fully differentiated eosinophil, a granular leukocyte with a nucleus that usually has two lobes connected by one or more slender threads, and cytoplasm containing coarse, round granules that are uniform in size and which can be stained by the dye eosin. Cells are also differentiated from other granulocytes by a small nuclear-to-cytoplasm ratio (1:3). This cell type is CD49d-positive.\")\n\n  Line 4142: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721601464\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12560239\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15514007\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000042 \"A myeloblast committed to the neutrophil lineage. This cell type is GATA-1 positive, C/EBPa-positive, AML-1-positive, c-myb-positive and has low expression of PU.1 transcription factor.\")\n\n  Line 4152: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721601464\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18466030\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19231594\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20837449\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.cap.org\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000043 \"A fully differentiated basophil, a granular leukocyte with an irregularly shaped, pale-staining nucleus that is partially constricted into two lobes, and with cytoplasm that contains coarse granules of variable size. Basophils contain vasoactive amines such as histamine and serotonin, which are released on appropriate stimulation.\")\n\n  Line 4211: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0878932437\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D023461\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000049 \"A progenitor cell committed to myeloid lineage, including the megakaryocyte and erythroid lineages.\")\n\n  Line 4230: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D055015\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16647566\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Megakaryocyte-erythroid_progenitor_cell\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000050 \"A progenitor cell committed to the megakaryocyte and erythroid lineages.\")\n\n  Line 4248: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:10407577\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16551251\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000051 \"A oligopotent progenitor cell committed to the lymphoid lineage.\")\n\n  Line 4265: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000052 \"A stem cell from which all cells of the body can form.\")\n\n  Line 4301: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D032446\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21849021\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000056 \"A cell that is commited to differentiating into a muscle cell.  Embryonic myoblasts develop from the mesoderm. They undergo proliferation, migrate to their various sites, and then differentiate into the appropriate form of myocytes.  Myoblasts also occur as transient populations of cells in muscles undergoing repair.\")\n\n  Line 4311: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0517223651\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D005347\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fibroblast\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000057 \"A connective tissue cell which secretes an extracellular matrix rich in collagen and other macromolecules. Flattened and irregular in outline with branching processes; appear fusiform or spindle-shaped.\")\n\n  Line 4325: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000034\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0618947256\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000058 \"Skeletogenic cell that is typically non-terminally differentiated, secretes an avascular, GAG rich matrix; is not buried in cartilage tissue matrix, retains the ability to divide, located adjacent to cartilage tissue (including within the perichondrium), and develops from prechondroblast (and thus prechondrogenic) cell.\")\n\n  Line 4337: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000034\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D000565\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000059 \"Skeletogenic cell that produces enamel, overlies the odontogenic papilla, and arises from the differentiation of a preameloblast cell.\")\n\n  Line 4354: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000034\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0618947256\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000060 \"Skeletogenic cell that secretes dentine matrix, is derived from the odontogenic papilla, and develops from a preodontoblast cell.\")\n\n  Line 4369: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000034\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0781733901\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000061 \"Skeletogenic cell that produces cementum (a bony substance that covers the root of a tooth), is part of the odontogenic papilla, and develops from a precementoblast cell.\")\n\n  Line 4383: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000034\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D010006\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000062 \"Skeletogenic cell that secretes osteoid, is capable of producing mineralized (hydroxyapatite) matrix, is located adjacent to or within osteoid tissue, and arises from the transformation of a preosteoblast cell.\")\n\n  Line 4395: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"FB:ma\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000063 \"OBSOLETE: A classification of cells by their microscopic appearance.\")\n\n  Line 4413: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"JB:jb\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34335193\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37008045\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9550134\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:/10.3389/fncel.2021.703951\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://www.britannica.com/science/ependymal-cell\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000065 \"A neuroepithelial glial cell, derived from a radial glial cell originating from the neuroectoderm, lines the ventricles of the brain and the central canal of the spinal cord. This cell is characterized by the presence of cilia on its apical surface, which can be motile or non-motile.\")\n\n  Line 4425: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"FB:ma\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D004847\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000066 \"A cell that is usually found in a two-dimensional sheet with a free surface. The cell has a cytoskeleton that allows for tight cell to cell contact and for cell polarity where apical part is directed towards the lumen and the basal part to the basal lamina.\")\n\n  Line 4485: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0471245208\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12662305\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000074 \"Obsolete. Use PO:0000066 from Plant Ontology instead. A cell that constitutes the mesophyll of a hydathode and is located between the xylem endings and the epidermis. Proposed to be involved in the retrieval of solutes from the xylem sap.\")\n\n  Line 4492: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO:0002065\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000075 \"A columnar/cuboidal epithelial cell is a cell usually found in a two dimensional sheet with a free surface. Columnar/cuboidal epithelial cells take on the shape of a column or cube.\")\n\n  Line 4504: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721662544\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26106328\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000077 \"A flat, squamous-like epithelial cell of mesodermal origin. It forms the mesothelium, which lines the body's serous cavities including the pleural, peritoneal, and pericardial spaces. This cell plays a crucial role in synthesizing and secreting lubricants, such as glycosaminoglycans and surfactants, which minimize friction between adjacent tissues during movement.\")\n\n  Line 4520: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Epithelium\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:/10.1016/B978-0-12-410424-2.00003-2\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://www.biologyonline.com/dictionary/stratified-epithelium\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000079 \"An epithelial cell, organized into multiple layers, with only the basal layer being in contact with the basement membrane.\")\n\n  Line 4533: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000081 \"A cell found predominately in the blood.\")\n\n  Line 4560: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0781735149\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000084 \"A type of lymphocyte whose defining characteristic is the expression of a T cell receptor complex.\")\n\n  Line 4627: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0517223651\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D007728\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15771589\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17105582\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000091 \"A tissue-resident macrophage of the reticuloendothelial system found on the luminal surface of the hepatic sinusoids involved in erythrocyte clearance. Markers include F4/80+, CD11b-low, CD68-positive, sialoadhesin-positive, CD163/SRCR-positive. Irregular, with long processes including lamellipodia extending into the sinusoid lumen, have flattened nucleus with cytoplasm containing characteristic invaginations of the plasma membrane (vermiform bodies); lie within the sinusoid lumen attached to the endothelial surface; derived from the bone marrow, form a major part of the body's mononuclear phagocyte system.\")\n\n  Line 4643: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0781735149\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:10428500\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15055519\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17380158\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000092 \"A specialized phagocytic cell associated with the absorption and removal of the mineralized matrix of bone tissue, which typically differentiates from monocytes. This cell has the following markers: tartrate-resistant acid phosphatase type 5-positive, PU.1-positive, c-fos-positive, nuclear factor NF-kappa-B p100 subunit-positive, tumor necrosis factor receptor superfamily member 11A-positive and macrophage colony-stimulating factor 1 receptor-positive.\")\n\n  Line 4666: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:amm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D006098\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Granulocyte\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000094 \"A leukocyte with abundant granules in the cytoplasm.\")\n\n  Line 4686: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D009504\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11138776\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12560239\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15514007\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:7880385\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.cap.org\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000096 \"A fully differentiated neutrophil, a granular leukocyte having a nucleus with three to five lobes connected by slender threads, and cytoplasm containing fine inconspicuous granules and stainable by neutral dyes. They are produced in bone marrow at a rate of 5e10-10e10/day and have a half-life of 6-8 hours. Neutrophils are CD15-positive, CD16-positive, CD32-positive, CD43-positive, CD181-positive, and CD182-positive.\")\n\n  Line 4707: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:068340007X\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D008407\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMCID:PMC1312421\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMCID:PMC2855166\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15153310\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16455980\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19671378\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:212366338\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9354811\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000097 \"A cell that is found in almost all tissues containing numerous basophilic granules and capable of releasing large amounts of histamine and heparin upon activation. Progenitors leave bone marrow and mature in connective and mucosal tissue. Mature mast cells are found in all tissues, except the bloodstream. Their phenotype is CD117-high, CD123-negative, CD193-positive, CD200R3-positive, and FceRI-high. Stem-cell factor (KIT-ligand; SCF) is the main controlling signal of their survival and development.\")\n\n  Line 4724: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0517223651\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721662544\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000098 \"A specialized epithelial cell involved in sensory perception. Restricted to special sense organs of the olfactory, gustatory, and vestibulocochlear receptor systems; contain sensory cells surrounded by supportive, non-receptive cells.\")\n\n  Line 4734: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D007395\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000099 \"Most generally any neuron which is not motor or sensory. Interneurons may also refer to neurons whose axons remain within a particular brain region as contrasted with projection neurons which have axons projecting to other brain regions.\")\n\n  Line 4745: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D009046\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16875686\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000100 \"An efferent neuron that passes from the central nervous system or a ganglion toward or to a muscle and conducts an impulse that causes or inhibits movement.\")\n\n  Line 4766: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23749412\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36381588\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000102 \"A neuron type that respond to multiple stimuli such as mechanical, thermal and chemical. This neuron type is responsible for integrating different types of sensory inputs, allowing organisms to respond appropriately to diverse environmental challenges.\")\n\n  Line 4773: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0444009442\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000103 \"A type of interneuron that has two neurites, usually an axon and a dendrite, extending from opposite poles of an ovoid cell body.\")\n\n  Line 4781: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"FMA:67287\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000104 \"A neuron with three or more neurites, usually an axon and multiple dendrites.\")\n\n  Line 4791: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"FMA:67305\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000105 \"Neuron with two neurites that are fused grossly when they protrude from the soma and bifurcate a short distance from the soma.\")\n\n  Line 4798: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"FMA:67278\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:nv\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000106 \"Neuron with one neurite that extends from the cell body.\")\n\n  Line 4831: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23040809\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1016/B978-012589762-4/50021-9\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000110 \"A neuron that uses neuropeptides as transmitters.\")\n\n  Line 4849: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34696823\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37608556\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000112 \"A neuron of the invertebrate central nervous system. This neuron innervates the central complex (CX) of an invertebrate brain and it forms columnar patterns with its dendrites. It is involved in navigation and spatial processing.\")\n\n  Line 4859: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0781735149\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000113 \"A vertebrate phagocyte with a single nucleus.\")\n\n  Line 4868: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:7892198\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Surface_ectoderm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:/10.1101/2024.07.02.601324\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000114 \"An ectodermal cell that is part of the external ectoderm, forming the outermost layer of the developing embryo. It is characterized by its polarized nature, with distinct apical and basal surfaces (Ferrante Jr., Reinke, & Stanley, 1995). Surface ectodermal cell gives rise to the epidermis, hair follicles, nails, sensory organs, and specialized structures like the apical ectodermal ridge crucial for limb development (Skoufa et al., 2024).\")\n\n  Line 4877: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D042783\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21275341\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Endothelial_cell\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://sourceforge.net/tracker/?func=detail&atid=440764&aid=3364936&group_id=36855\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000115 \"An endothelial cell comprises the outermost layer or lining of anatomical structures and can be squamous or cuboidal. In mammals, endothelial cell has vimentin filaments and is derived from the mesoderm.\")\n\n  Line 4889: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:cvs\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000116 \"Pioneer neurons establish a pathway in the developing central nervous system and then undergo programmed cell death once the adult axons, which follow them, have made connections with the target site. Thus, they are a transient cell type involved in axon guidance.\")\n\n  Line 4933: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D011689\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12907269\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:14568361\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31424738\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33288911\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:38168772\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000121 \"An inhibitory neuron and the sole output neuron of the cerebellar cortex, the Purkinje cell's soma is located between the granular and molecular layers of the cerebellum. It is one of the largest neural cells in the mammalian brain, ranging from 50 to 80 micrometres in diameter. Purkinje cells have planar, fan-shaped dendrites that branch extensively with little overlap. This cell type receives synaptic input from parallel fibres, which modulate high-frequency spike activity known as \\\"simple spikes,\\\" and climbing fibres, which modulate infrequent calcium spike activity known as \\\"complex spikes\\\". Purkinje cells are involved in motor coordination, particularly in correcting movements in progress.\")\n\n  Line 4985: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721662544\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000126 \"A neuroglial cell of ectodermal origin, i.e., the astrocytes and oligodendrocytes considered together.\")\n\n  Line 4997: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D001253\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11746784\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12162730\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12898703\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20942978\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Astrocyte\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000127 \"A class of large neuroglial (macroglial) cells in the central nervous system - the largest and most numerous neuroglial cells in the brain and spinal cord. Astrocytes (from 'star' cells) are irregularly shaped with many long processes, including those with 'end feet' which form the glial (limiting) membrane and directly and indirectly contribute to the blood-brain barrier. They regulate the extracellular ionic and chemical environment, and 'reactive astrocytes' (along with microglia) respond to injury.\")\n\n  Line 5008: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D009836\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oligodendrocyte\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000128 \"A class of large neuroglial (macroglial) cells in the central nervous system. Form the insulating myelin sheath of axons in the central nervous system.\")\n\n  Line 5023: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721601464\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D017628\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11517395\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12430718\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:14561199\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:14612429\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16177057\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19461673\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:2089275\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microglia\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000129 \"A transcriptomically distinct central nervous system macrophage found in the parenchyma of the central nervous system. Marker include CD11b-positive, F4/80-positive, and CD68-positive.\")\n\n  Line 5055: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21976958\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23284695\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34741068\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36769303\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000132 \"An hexagonal, flattened, mitochondria-rich endothelial cell that forms a monolayer on the posterior surface of the cornea (the corneal endothelium). Corneal endothelial cells are derived from the neural crest and are responsible for keeping the cornea transparent by maintaining the tissue in a semi-dry state through the action of their ionic pumps and tight junction barrier.\")\n\n  Line 5065: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:068340007X\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000133 \"Ectoderm destined to be nervous tissue.\")\n\n  Line 5072: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"FB:ma\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMCID:PMC2613570\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:10102814\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16923606\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17986482\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19960544\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mesenchymal_stem_cell\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.copewithcytokines.de/cope.cgi?key=mesenchymal%20stem%20cells\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000134 \"A connective tissue cell that normally gives rise to other cells that are organized as three-dimensional masses. In humans, this cell type is CD73-positive, CD90-positive, CD105-positive, CD45-negative, CD34-negative, and MHCII-negative. They may further differentiate into osteoblasts, adipocytes, myocytes, neurons, or chondroblasts in vitro. Originally described as residing in the bone marrow, this cell type is now known to reside in many, if not all, adult organs.\")\n\n  Line 5096: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20303382\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20305780\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29286323\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31473260\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32084275\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9177213\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:/10.1186/1755-1536-5-S1-S6\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000135 \"A bone marrow-derived cell that predominantly develops from myeloid lineage-restricted progenitor cells and circulates in peripheral blood, characterized by co-expression of hematopoietic markers CD45 and CD34 along with stromal markers including collagen type I in both humans and mice (Chesney et al., 1997; Blakaj and Bucala, 2012). This spindle-shaped cell exhibits a unique dual identity, functionally bridging immune and stromal compartments with characteristics of both monocytes and fibroblasts. Predominantly arising from circulating monocytes, it migrates to injury sites via chemokine receptors and participates in wound repair through extracellular matrix deposition, cytokine secretion, and antigen presentation via MHC class II. As mesenchymal progenitors, fibrocytes can differentiate into fibroblasts, myofibroblasts, and adipocytes, contributing to both physiological repair and pathological fibrosis (Blakaj and Bucala, 2012).\")\n\n  Line 5123: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D010011\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000137 \"A mature osteoblast that has become embedded in the bone matrix. They occupy a small cavity, called lacuna, in the matrix and are connected to adjacent osteocytes via protoplasmic projections called canaliculi.\")\n\n  Line 5137: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000034\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D019902\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000138 \"Skeletogenic cell that is terminally differentiated, secretes an avascular, GAG-rich matrix, is embedded in cartilage tissue matrix, retains the ability to divide, and develops from a chondroblast cell.\")\n\n  Line 5176: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19073178\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000142 \"A cell occurring in the peripheral part of the vitreous body of the eye that may be responsible for production of hyaluronic acid and collagen.\")\n\n  Line 5200: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0781735149\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000145 \"A cell capable of processing and presenting lipid and protein antigens to T cells in order to initiate an immune response.\")\n\n  Line 5241: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ORCID:0000-0002-7073-9172\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000150 \"An epithelial cell, located in a gland, that is specialised for the synthesis and secretion of specific biomolecules, such as hormones, or mucous.\")\n\n  Line 5250: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721662544\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000151 \"A cell that specializes in controlled release of one or more substances.\")\n\n  Line 5280: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21907708\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30571046\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Gastric_chief_cell\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000155 \"An epithelial cell of the stomach that is part of the fundic gastric gland. This cell is characterized by a basally located nucleus, abundant rough endoplasmic reticulum, and large apical secretory granules. It produces and secretes pepsinogen, the inactive precursor of the digestive enzyme pepsin.\")\n\n  Line 5301: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721662544\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000157 \"A cell that specializes in secretion of surfactant in the alveoli of the lung.\")\n\n  Line 5308: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"DOI:10.1183/09031936.00146609\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"DOI:10.1378/chest.12-2762\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28128362\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29874100\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:7905712\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000158 \"A non-mucous, epithelial secretory cell that is part of the tracheobronchial tree. A club cell has short microvilli but no cilia. A club cell is able to multiply and differentiate into ciliated cells to regenerate the bronchiolar epithelium and it also protects the tracheobronchial epithelium.\")\n\n  Line 5326: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D020397\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goblet_cell\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000160 \"A specialized, columnar, mucus secreting epithelial cell shaped like a flask or goblet. A narrow basal end contains the nucleus while the apical end is swollen by the accumulation of mucus laden secretory granules.  Short microvilli project from the apical plasma membrane.\")\n\n  Line 5347: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0517223651\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31613538\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31670611\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000162 \"An epithelial cell of the stomach that is part of the fundic gastric gland. This cell is characterized by its pyramidal shape, abundant mitochondria, and a complex network of secretory canaliculi lined with microvilli. It secretes hydrochloric acid into the stomach lumen and produces intrinsic factor, essential for vitamin B12 absorption.\")\n\n  Line 5372: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"SANBI:mhl\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000164 \"An endocrine cell that is located in the epithelium of the gastrointestinal tract or in the pancreas.\")\n\n  Line 5420: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0517223651\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pancreatic_b_cell\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000169 \"A cell that secretes insulin and is located towards the center of the islets of Langerhans.\")\n\n  Line 5453: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721662544\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000171 \"A type A enteroendocrine cell found in the periphery of the islets of Langerhans that secretes glucagon.\")\n\n  Line 5471: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"FMA:0517223651\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000173 \"A D cell located in the pancreas. Peripherally placed within the islets like type A cells; contains somatostatin.\")\n\n  Line 5493: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D008184\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31849844\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000175 \"A progesterone secreting cell in the corpus luteum. The large luteal cells develop from the granulosa cells. The small luteal cells develop from the theca cells.\")\n\n  Line 5515: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12050120\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000178 \"A Leydig cell is a testosterone-secreting cell in the interstitial area, between the seminiferous tubules, in the testis.\")\n\n  Line 5550: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0412046911\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D022781\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19717280\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hepatocyte\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000182 \"The main structural component of the liver. They are specialized epithelial cells that are organized into interconnected plates called lobules. Majority of cell population of liver, polygonal in shape, arranged in plates or trabeculae between sinusoids; may have single nucleus or binucleated.\")\n\n  Line 5577: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721662544\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000185 \"Contractile cells resembling smooth muscle cells that are present in glands, notably the mammary gland, and aid in secretion. This cell has long weaving dendritic processes containing myofilament.\")\n\n  Line 5589: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D058628\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19800625\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20630469\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22387320\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000186 \"An animal cell that has characteristics of both a fibroblast cell and a smooth muscle cell.\")\n\n  Line 5624: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0323052908\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000189 \"A muscle cell that develops tension more slowly than a fast-twitch fiber.\")\n\n  Line 5632: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC